WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.130
- [Narrator] These are just a fraction

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.850
of the 23 million
Flowers 1-800-FLOWERS.COM

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.040
needs to get from farm to florist

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.720
to customer for Mother's Day.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.540
with 10% of the annual revenue on the line

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.220
there's little room for error.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.830
It's the company's biggest
day for Floral sales.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.600
- It is our Super Bowl.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.760
- [Narrator] This distribution
center in New York City

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.340
will see 10,000 of those
Mother's Day orders.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.740
It's just one of the
thousands of facilities

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.200
and independent floors
the company depends on

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.783
to get fresh Flowers to
customers nationwide.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.380
We visited the company's
busiest hub to understand

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.150
the complicated logistics behind

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.550
Florals biggest day of the year.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.303
This is the economics
of 1-800-FLOWERS.COM.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.810
In the 1980s, Flowers
were typically purchased

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.340
at a neighborhood grocery store

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.440
or a local florist like this one.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.371
- When you have something to say

00:00:51.371 --> 00:00:52.500
Floral Plenty can help you say with style.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.020
- [Narrator] But in 1986,
that New York florist

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.550
purchased a toll-free number

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.043
setting in motion a transformation
of the industry just

00:00:59.043 --> 00:01:01.530
- [Announcer] Just call
on in or visit our stores.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.750
- When we acquired the
1-800-FLOWERS number

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.270
we became a national business overnight.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.250
- [Narrator] The company
grew into a large network

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.083
of florists across the country.

00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:12.690
Just call the number and it
would figure out the details

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.370
and then came the worldwide web.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.380
In the 1990s, the floral industry

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.150
was one of the first to go online

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.700
with 1-800-FLOWERS leading the pack.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.980
- We can take care of that
right now with America Online.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:23.820
- We can?

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.320
- Yeah, we can send your mom Flowers.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.210
- They're very cutting edge in technology

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.470
and online technology.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:31.740
I would consider them a leader
as an e-commerce company.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.990
- [Narrator] As a research
analyst, Linda Bolton Weiser

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.750
has covered 1-800-FLOWERS
for over a decade.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.854
- The floral network
is key to the business

00:01:39.854 --> 00:01:43.656
and sort of standardizing the brand

00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:48.060
to be able to advertise is
really part of what they did

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.690
to pioneer the industry

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.820
- [Announcer] Better call 1-800-FLOWERS.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.237
- [Narrator] Today the company brings in

00:01:55.237 --> 00:01:57.600
$2 billion in annual revenue

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.300
and with more than 5,000
florists in its network

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.640
holiday logistics are pretty complicated.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.590
- Preparing for Mother's,
Day is one of those things

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.270
that really gets our blood going.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.370
- [Narrator] After customer
places an order online

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.470
it can be sent to a few different places.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.580
A farm, a distribution center owned

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.750
by the company or one of the
network's local florists.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.550
Where and how orders are fulfilled

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.950
depends on the type of
product and the location

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.000
of the customer.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.640
- Getting the Flowers
to the right recipient

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.530
is more complex than people think.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.360
- [Narrator] It all starts
at a farm like this one

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.000
where Flowers for the
holiday are harvested in May.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.340
Every year the company
relies on its own data

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.950
to forecast what types of
Flowers they'll need planted.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.650
- Preparation for a major
holiday like Mother's Day

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.020
really began a year ago when we would work

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.647
with all of our suppliers to say,

00:02:41.647 --> 00:02:43.860
"Here's what we're thinking of designing.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.080
How does that match your growing cycles?"

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.158
- [Narrator] The company imports Flowers

00:02:48.158 --> 00:02:49.980
from all over the world
including California,

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.110
Ecuador, Holland and Thailand.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.420
Roses are the most
popular for Mother's Day.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.840
The company expects to
deliver 10 million in 2023.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.290
At the farms Flowers are
cut sorted by type and color

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.760
and packaged for shipping.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.540
The hardest part, keeping
Flowers alive and looking fresh.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.970
Some customers have complained
that their orders arrived

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.620
looking worse for wear.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.180
- [Customer] This is how they came.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.100
The Flowers were dead.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.110
- [Narrator] The company
says that customer experience

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.600
is its number one priority
and that when it might

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.730
miss the mark, it works with urgency

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.190
to rectify the situation
quickly and to ensure

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.700
the customer is 100%
happy with the resolution.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.280
But the most important thing
to avoid those dead Flowers

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.680
in the first place, keep them cold,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.410
including on refrigerated
trucks that cart the Flowers

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:35.730
all over the country.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.400
- The fast you can get
that cut flower down

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.990
to about 33, 34 degrees and
then maintain that temperature

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:45.240
you suspend life and you can really extend

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.183
the vase life that a
customer therefore gets.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.456
- [Narrator] The Flowers are kept cold

00:03:52.456 --> 00:03:53.910
through transportation and
arrival of distribution centers

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:55.470
like this one in New York.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.960
Warehouse manager, Isaiah
Brown and his staff

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:01.020
are preparing to receive
hundreds of thousands of Flowers

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.000
more than double what they usually get.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.790
- When he product comes in
for the week of Mother's Day

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.440
we want to get it in
in as late as possible

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.600
so it's at as freshest for our customers.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.262
- [Narrator] Which means
all of the Mother's Day Prep

00:04:12.262 --> 00:04:13.095
has to happen fast.

00:04:13.095 --> 00:04:16.080
The staff here almost triples
to prepare for the rush.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.360
The Flowers are unpacked and processed.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.180
- It's very important that
we strip bottom leaves

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.580
so that those leaves
when the Flowers are cut

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.343
and put in the buckets are
not submerged in the water.

00:04:27.196 --> 00:04:29.280
- [Narrator] Cutting
these stems at an angle

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.920
allows water to flow to
the heads of the Flowers.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.300
After Flowers are processed,

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.980
they're returned to the cooler room.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.050
Designers pop in and
out to pick out Flowers

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.340
for their arrangements.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.920
This team in New York will
make a couple thousand Bouquets

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.020
every day for the week of Mother's. Day

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.690
- It could take any
matter from a few minutes

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.760
till 15 minutes.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.140
It all depends on the occasion

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.420
and the type of bouquet
we're talking about.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.918
- [Narrator] When the designers finish,

00:04:53.918 --> 00:04:55.230
most of the arrangements
will be loaded into trucks

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:56.923
like this one and delivered
to the customer's door

00:04:56.923 --> 00:04:57.756
on the same day.

00:04:57.756 --> 00:04:58.850
- Go Flowers delivery.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.810
- [Narrator] Sometimes
other gifts like teddy bears

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.028
or chocolate covered strawberries

00:05:06.028 --> 00:05:08.100
or fruit Bouquets are
delivered with the Flowers.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.140
That's part of the
company's bigger strategy

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.940
to become a one stop gift shop

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.490
where customers can also
order from Harry &amp; David

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:15.810
or Sherry's Berries.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.963
- They would like to be known

00:05:17.963 --> 00:05:21.510
as the premier online gifting marketplace.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:24.720
- [Narrator] In fact, 45%
of the company's business

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.150
is in gourmet foods and gift baskets.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.631
Business boomed during the pandemic

00:05:29.631 --> 00:05:31.410
as people stayed home
and sent gifts online.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.120
But as the world came out of lockdown

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.890
and an economic downturn loomed

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.440
both revenues and profits decreased.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.110
- Flowers are considered in ephemeral gift

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.780
meaning you can't actually
use it or consume it.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.880
It's just for beauty and enjoyment.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.630
And so in a recession that
tends to be the gift class

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.580
that falls off first.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.950
- [Narrator] Inflation and
rising labor and supply costs

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.780
have also affected the company.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.780
Competition has blossomed
too with companies like

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.360
Bouqs, UrbanStems and Farmgirl Flowers

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.153
entering the $12 billion
Floral gifting market.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.569
Food delivery services
like DoorDash and Uber Eats

00:06:06.569 --> 00:06:07.402
are also getting in on the action.

00:06:07.402 --> 00:06:09.210
- We work with many of them, even though

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.590
they also compete against us.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.810
E-commerce gives the ability for people

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.200
to get into your category relatively easy.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.270
It doesn't replace the
50 years of experience

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.530
that we bring to the table.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.580
- [Narrator] To keep an edge,

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.580
McCann is once again looking
to emerging technologies.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:27.270
In April, the company launched
an AI generated poem composer

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.400
that's powered by ChatGBT.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.737
- [Chris McCann] I see opportunity to grow

00:06:31.737 --> 00:06:33.960
exactly as we are now but
I know that technology

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.570
is going to change things and
we'll look a lot different

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.120
than we do five years from now.

00:06:39.761 --> 00:06:41.735
(bright music)

